## Privilege Escalation – UAC Bypass via SilentCleanup Task (T1548.002)
## Splunk searches used during investigation

## 1. Reduce Atomic Red Team framework module noise
index="win1_log" earliest="09/28/2026:15:30:31" NOT "C:\\Users\\host1\\Documents\\WindowsPowerShell\\Modules\\Invoke-AtomicRedTeam\\2.3.0\\"

## 2. Broad search for any resulting powershell/cmd process (no parent-image assumption) Returned only the original batch-file execution - confirmed absence of a resulting elevated process
index="win1_log" earliest="09/28/2026:15:30:31" (Image="*\\powershell.exe" OR Image="*\\cmd.exe")
| table _time, Image, ParentImage, ParentProcessId, ProcessId, CommandLine, IntegrityLevel


## Native OS diagnostic commands (run locally on the VM, outside Splunk) --------
## Task run history and last result code
schtasks /query /tn "\Microsoft\Windows\DiskCleanup\SilentCleanup" /v /fo list
## Task full configuration (Principal / RunLevel / SecurityDescriptor)
schtasks /query /tn "\Microsoft\Windows\DiskCleanup\SilentCleanup" /xml
## Confirm task registration / exact name
Get-ScheduledTask -TaskPath "\Microsoft\Windows\DiskCleanup\"
